WEBVTT

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:02.648
Words in context.

00:00:02.648 --> 00:00:05.003
Predict your own word before you look.

00:00:05.003 --> 00:00:06.861
The passage always hands you a clue.

00:00:08.414 --> 00:00:10.229
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:10.229 --> 00:00:14.399
A blank, or an underlined word, in a short passage.

00:00:14.399 --> 00:00:16.423
And four single words to choose from.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.545
It isn't testing whether you know fancy words.

00:00:20.545 --> 00:00:23.339
It's testing the precise meaning this sentence needs.

00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:25.866
Here's the method.

00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:30.391
First, read the whole passage, not just the sentence with the blank.

00:00:30.391 --> 00:00:31.791
Find the clue.

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:34.616
Words like but and although flip the meaning.

00:00:34.616 --> 00:00:38.151
A colon, or because, keeps it the same.

00:00:38.151 --> 00:00:42.196
Now predict your own simple word, before you look at the choices.

00:00:42.196 --> 00:00:43.606
Then match it.

00:00:43.606 --> 00:00:47.448
Check the direction, positive or negative, and the strength.

00:00:48.527 --> 00:00:50.252
Four clue rules.

00:00:50.252 --> 00:00:55.997
Contrast clues, like although and but, mean the blank is the opposite of the other idea.

00:00:55.997 --> 00:01:02.392
Restatement clues, like a colon or a dash, mean the blank repeats an idea that's already there.

00:01:02.392 --> 00:01:03.827
Match the tone.

00:01:03.827 --> 00:01:07.517
If the passage is critical, the word can't be a compliment.

00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:11.032
And for underlined words, beware the common meaning.

00:01:11.032 --> 00:01:12.613
Qualified can mean limited.

00:01:13.626 --> 00:01:15.071
Let's try one.

00:01:15.071 --> 00:01:20.371
The word although sets up a contrast with her later work, which was remarkably consistent.

00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:23.351
So the blank must mean the opposite of consistent.

00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:27.766
Right after the blank, we read: results that differed every time.

00:01:27.766 --> 00:01:30.976
So predict a simple word, like unreliable.

00:01:30.976 --> 00:01:32.276
Now match it.

00:01:32.276 --> 00:01:34.561
Influential is positive.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.026
Inexpensive is about cost.

00:01:37.026 --> 00:01:39.146
Meticulous means careful.

00:01:39.146 --> 00:01:42.619
Inconsistent matches unreliable, so the answer is A.

00:01:43.706 --> 00:01:45.886
Watch out for the topic word.

00:01:45.886 --> 00:01:53.116
It sounds related to science, or art, or whatever the passage is about, but it doesn't fit the logic.

00:01:53.116 --> 00:01:55.357
Match your prediction, not the topic.

00:01:56.414 --> 00:02:03.309
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the clue rules, and the trap.

00:02:03.309 --> 00:02:06.183
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
